  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "m28-s001",
      "speakerId": "m28-spk-a",
      "startMs": 0,
      "endMs": 4400,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Thanks all. This is scoping for the Building 5 expansion."
    },
    {
      "id": "m28-s002",
      "speakerId": "m28-spk-b",
      "startMs": 4650,
      "endMs": 11330,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "For context, NWR's board approved the budget in principle. I need to confirm the final number."
    },
    {
      "id": "m28-s003",
      "speakerId": "m28-spk-c",
      "startMs": 11580,
      "endMs": 15600,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "The platform side is ready, the cluster has room."
    },
    {
      "id": "m28-s004",
      "speakerId": "m28-spk-a",
      "startMs": 15850,
      "endMs": 18350,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "What's different about Building 5?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m28-s005",
      "speakerId": "m28-spk-d",
      "startMs": 18600,
      "endMs": 25280,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "It's bigger, and the shelving is older. The location data will be messier than Building 3."
    },
    {
      "id": "m28-s006",
      "speakerId": "m28-spk-e",
      "startMs": 25530,
      "endMs": 31450,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "And the pickers there have never used zones. Building 3 pickers had peak-season experience."
    },
    {
      "id": "m28-s007",
      "speakerId": "m28-spk-b",
      "startMs": 31700,
      "endMs": 34960,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Do we keep the same layout approach?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m28-s008",
      "speakerId": "m28-spk-d",
      "startMs": 35210,
      "endMs": 42650,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'd keep the same zone picking layout. Changing two things at once makes it impossible to learn anything."
    },
    {
      "id": "m28-s009",
      "speakerId": "m28-spk-b",
      "startMs": 42900,
      "endMs": 48060,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Agreed. Building 5 uses the same zone picking layout as Building 3."
    },
    {
      "id": "m28-s010",
      "speakerId": "m28-spk-a",
      "startMs": 48310,
      "endMs": 51570,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Decided. What do you need first, Tomás?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m28-s011",
      "speakerId": "m28-spk-d",
      "startMs": 51820,
      "endMs": 57740,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "A sensor survey. I'll finish the sensor survey of Building 5 by August 7."
    },
    {
      "id": "m28-s012",
      "speakerId": "m28-spk-b",
      "startMs": 57990,
      "endMs": 62010,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'll confirm the budget by the end of July."
    },
    {
      "id": "m28-s013",
      "speakerId": "m28-spk-a",
      "startMs": 62260,
      "endMs": 64760,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Chloé, what about the pickers?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m28-s014",
      "speakerId": "m28-spk-e",
      "startMs": 65010,
      "endMs": 71690,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'll run the same training we did in Building 3, in French and English this time."
    },
    {
      "id": "m28-s015",
      "speakerId": "m28-spk-c",
      "startMs": 71940,
      "endMs": 76340,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "When does Building 5 actually open for the new shifts?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m28-s016",
      "speakerId": "m28-spk-b",
      "startMs": 76590,
      "endMs": 83650,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Building 5 opens for the new flow in Q4, but I don't have a firmer date yet."
    },
    {
      "id": "m28-s017",
      "speakerId": "m28-spk-a",
      "startMs": 83900,
      "endMs": 86400,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "We'll plan to Q4 then."
    },
    {
      "id": "m28-s018",
      "speakerId": "m28-spk-c",
      "startMs": 86650,
      "endMs": 89910,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Chloé, do you report to Sarah now?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m28-s019",
      "speakerId": "m28-spk-e",
      "startMs": 90160,
      "endMs": 94940,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Yes, since the spring. Floor supervisors all report to Sarah directly."
    },
    {
      "id": "m28-s020",
      "speakerId": "m28-spk-a",
      "startMs": 95190,
      "endMs": 98450,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Tomás, how are weekends? You mentioned coaching."
    },
    {
      "id": "m28-s021",
      "speakerId": "m28-spk-d",
      "startMs": 98700,
      "endMs": 104240,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I coach my daughter's football team on Saturdays, so no weekend cutovers please."
    },
    {
      "id": "m28-s022",
      "speakerId": "m28-spk-b",
      "startMs": 104490,
      "endMs": 106990,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Nobody wants weekend cutovers anyway."
    },
    {
      "id": "m28-s023",
      "speakerId": "m28-spk-a",
      "startMs": 107240,
      "endMs": 114300,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Great. So: same layout, sensor survey by August 7, budget by end of July, opening in Q4."
    }
  ],
  "note": {
    "version": 1,
    "body": "# Northwind Building 5 expansion scoping\n\n**Date:** July 16\n**Attendees:** Alex Rivera (Larkspur Labs), Sarah Chen (Northwind Robotics), Owen Barker (Northwind Robotics), Tomás Aguilar (Northwind Robotics), Chloé Dubois (Northwind Robotics)\n\n## Summary\n\nScoping for the Building 5 expansion, which extends the pick-path approach from Building 3. NWR's board has approved the budget in principle; Sarah needs to confirm the final number.\n\n## Differences from Building 3\n\n- Building 5 is bigger and has older shelving, so location data will be messier.\n- Building 5 pickers have never used zones; Building 3 pickers had peak-season experience.\n- The platform cluster has room for Building 5.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- **Building 5 uses the same zone picking layout as Building 3**, so the team changes only one thing at a time.\n- No weekend cutovers.\n\n## Timeline\n\nBuilding 5 opens for the new flow in Q4; there is no firmer date yet.\n\n## Action items\n\n- **Tomás Aguilar** — finish the sensor survey of Building 5 by August 7.\n- **Sarah Chen** — confirm the budget by the end of July.\n- **Chloé Dubois** — run the Building 3 picker training in Building 5, in French and English.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Floor supervisors, including Chloé, have reported directly to Sarah since the spring.\n- Tomás coaches his daughter's football team on Saturdays.\n"
  },
